    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0208",
      "sequence": 220,
      "meaning": "Hearing words so unwelcome, the king’s heart shook and his face lost its color. ‘In old age I obtained these four sons; your Brahmin words were not spoken after reflection. Ask for land, cows, wealth or treasury—I shall gladly give everything today. Nothing is dearer than body and life, and even those I would give you in an instant. All my sons are dear as life, but I cannot give Rāma, lord. How can this supremely tender, beautiful boy face those dreadful, cruel demons?’ Hearing the king’s love-soaked speech, the wise sage inwardly rejoiced. Vasiṣṭha then counselled the king in many ways until his doubt vanished. With great honor Daśaratha summoned both sons, embraced and instructed them, and said, ‘You two, lords of my life, now have no father but the sage.’ Giving many blessings, he entrusted them to the seer. The Lords went to their mothers’ quarters and then departed after bowing their heads at the mothers’ feet. Joyfully the two heroes went to remove the sage’s fear—the lion-like men, oceans of mercy and steadfast causes of the whole universe.",
